  "scope": "binary32 raw words under round-to-nearest-even; controls are finite normal or signed zero, with no exception-flag assertions",
  "derivation_tags": {
    "zero-y-axis": "Positive X returns Y signed zero. Negative X returns signed source pi representative: Apple low 40490fda, Sun/modern high 40490fdb.",
    "near-half-k70": "Exact scale-invariant |y/x|=2^70. Apple/modern F64 half-pi offset rounds high. Sun k=70 shortcut z rounds high, but negative-X reconstruction pi-(z-low) rounds half-pi low.",
    "zero-x-axis": "All three return signed half-pi high 3fc90fdb independently of X zero sign.",
    "equal-magnitude": "Positive X gives signed pi/4 high 3f490fdb; negative X gives signed 3pi/4 4016cbe4. Sun id=1 reduction is exact zero.",
    "zero-origin": "Positive X zero returns signed Y zero; negative X zero selects each source pi representative with Y sign.",
    "apple-ratio-2^-22-neighbor": "Y words 347fffff,34800000,34800001 over |X|=1 bracket the <=2^-22 guard. Negative-X result rounds 40490fda for all sources on both branches. Positive-X atan(Y) rounds Y exactly.",
    "sun-k60-neighbor": "Y=3f000000 with |X|=207fffff,20800000,20800001 gives arithmetic-shift k=61,61,60. Shortcut versus atanf saturation both yield high half-pi before quadrant reconstruction; Sun negative-X result is low while Apple/modern are high."
  },
